  "summary_en": "UN Secretary-General's report consolidating Member State and stakeholder submissions under resolution 78/241 on lethal autonomous weapons systems. It covers definitions, humanitarian, legal, security, technological and ethical concerns, and next steps, and renews the call for a legally binding instrument by 2026 that prohibits and regulates such systems.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "No agreed international definition of LAWS exists; the ICRC working definition is widely used.",
   "Many States support a two-tier approach: prohibit systems that cannot comply with IHL, regulate the rest.",
   "Human control is essential for accountability and compliance with IHL.",
   "The Secretary-General calls for a legally binding instrument by 2026.",
   "Some States consider existing IHL sufficient and oppose new binding rules."
